WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:07.806
- Hi, what a do.

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.734
Welcome to another episode of Real Mature.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:12.374
It's a show we make about
things you do when you grow up.

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:14.440
And one of the things you
do when you grow up is

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.576
you get to know your
family in a different way.

00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:19.177
So we have three different videos we made

00:00:19.177 --> 00:00:21.429
about people getting
to know their families.

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:23.914
And the first one kinda starts with me,

00:00:23.914 --> 00:00:26.096
so that's why there's
like no one else here.

00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:28.183
But usually there's another person.

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:30.156
So we're just gonna get into it.

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:31.039
You guys ready?

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:31.944
You ready Jenny?

00:00:31.944 --> 00:00:32.989
You ready?

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:34.568
Boom, let's do it.

00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:37.183
(funky jazz music)

00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:42.505
- So the first video we
want to show you actually

00:00:42.505 --> 00:00:44.479
started with another, much worse,

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:47.543
idea for a video that our team had.

00:00:47.543 --> 00:00:50.296
Basically, my parents are
coming into the office.

00:00:50.296 --> 00:00:52.664
I manage this team, and everyone was like,

00:00:52.664 --> 00:00:54.754
"Wouldn't it be funny if we make a video

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:59.235
"where we get to ask Henry's
parents questions about Henry?"

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:01.464
- I'd love to see your impressions of him.

00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:02.973
"Hey, I'm Henry!"

00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:04.599
- Oh, no no, my impression of Henry,

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:06.526
I don't have my phone, is texting.

00:01:06.526 --> 00:01:08.151
- On a scale of one to ten,

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.937
how much do you want Henry to get married?

00:01:11.897 --> 00:01:13.034
- Retell.

00:01:13.034 --> 00:01:13.797
- Really?

00:01:13.797 --> 00:01:14.981
- So one interesting thing happened,

00:01:14.981 --> 00:01:18.208
which is our friend Mark
didn't really understand

00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:19.787
the idea of the thing.

00:01:19.787 --> 00:01:22.040
He didn't ask my parents
an embarrassing question,

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.221
he just asked a question he
wanted to know about life.

00:01:25.221 --> 00:01:28.263
And my parents kinda had like
a really interesting answer.

00:01:28.263 --> 00:01:30.515
- Is it worth having kids?

00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:32.164
- Of course it is.

00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:34.741
There's nothing in the world like it.

00:01:34.741 --> 00:01:37.225
- Every parent, I hear
every parent say that

00:01:37.225 --> 00:01:38.572
about having kids.

00:01:39.812 --> 00:01:41.849
Like, the tough parts.

00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:47.052
- A downside is every parent

00:01:47.052 --> 00:01:49.530
worries some about their kids.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.105
You know, wants them to have a good life.

00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:53.195
Wants them to be happy.

00:01:53.195 --> 00:01:55.888
When things don't go well for them,

00:01:55.888 --> 00:01:57.745
they don't go well for parents.

00:01:59.255 --> 00:02:01.221
That's a reflection of love,

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.845
but it's also sometimes tough.

00:02:03.845 --> 00:02:05.169
- We thought it'd be interesting

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:08.025
if we just got people
to call their parents

00:02:08.025 --> 00:02:10.254
and ask them a question
they never thought to ask

00:02:10.254 --> 00:02:12.668
and see if we could all
learn something about life.

00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:14.712
Hanging out, get to know our
parents a little bit better.

00:02:14.712 --> 00:02:17.196
And first, we have a
video that Colin made.

00:02:17.196 --> 00:02:18.682
Colin, tell us about our video.

00:02:18.682 --> 00:02:21.097
- We got contacted by a
woman who got thrown into

00:02:21.097 --> 00:02:23.163
a pretty interesting living dynamic

00:02:23.163 --> 00:02:25.694
where she got to know
her siblings pretty well.

00:02:25.694 --> 00:02:26.948
- You wanna give us more?

00:02:26.948 --> 00:02:27.876
That's kinda vague.

00:02:27.876 --> 00:02:29.409
- That was pretty vague.

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:30.918
- I liked it, I thought it was good.

00:02:30.918 --> 00:02:32.984
- Okay, well then, just
cut to the video then.

00:02:32.984 --> 00:02:34.122
(laughs)

00:02:34.122 --> 00:02:35.330
- Fine.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.159
- [Isabel] So this time last year,

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:41.425
I was working full time.

00:02:41.425 --> 00:02:43.538
I was living in my own apartment

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:45.233
with my two best friends,

00:02:45.233 --> 00:02:48.530
and just kinda had a normal life.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.922
Priority was all just kind of about work

00:02:50.922 --> 00:02:54.549
and doing that early 20
thing of trying to move up.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:56.351
I was doing that.

00:02:56.351 --> 00:02:59.184
I got a call from a friend who
was over at my dad's house.

00:02:59.184 --> 00:03:00.995
He's been sick since
I was seven years old.

00:03:00.995 --> 00:03:03.619
It kept going up and down,
he had prostate cancer.

00:03:03.619 --> 00:03:05.824
So I didn't necessarily
think it was a big deal,

00:03:05.824 --> 00:03:07.032
I thought she was just getting nervous

00:03:07.032 --> 00:03:08.773
about the way he always was.

00:03:08.773 --> 00:03:09.772
But everything changed.

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:13.835
I left my job, my mother just
wasn't capable of parenting.

00:03:13.835 --> 00:03:15.089
Before he went into the hospital,

00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:17.086
my dad had asked me to
take care of the twins

00:03:17.086 --> 00:03:18.704
if he passed away.

00:03:18.704 --> 00:03:21.206
(light piano music)

00:03:24.342 --> 00:03:26.292
- Nobody that I know is being raised

00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:27.848
by their sisters.

00:03:27.848 --> 00:03:29.580
Which I guess is pretty cool.

00:03:31.931 --> 00:03:33.927
- I was definitely, for
lack of better terms,

00:03:33.927 --> 00:03:36.565
probably a little bit
more on the selfish side.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.928
- Charlotte had actually
moved home to save up money

00:03:45.928 --> 00:03:47.530
to travel around the world.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.177
- And so now I'm sharing a
room with a 15-year-old girl.

00:03:50.177 --> 00:03:51.454
And it's different.

00:03:51.454 --> 00:03:53.195
- So obviously in this day and age,

00:03:53.195 --> 00:03:54.449
if you're faced with a problem,

00:03:54.449 --> 00:03:56.376
the first thing you do is Google.

00:03:56.376 --> 00:03:58.652
And there was nothing there.

00:03:58.652 --> 00:04:00.254
- I think that's actually why Izzie

00:04:00.254 --> 00:04:02.181
started doing the blog.

00:04:02.181 --> 00:04:05.084
Also because she couldn't
find anything online.

00:04:05.084 --> 00:04:06.454
- Just talk about what we're doing,

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:08.427
so next time someone
else goes through this,

00:04:08.427 --> 00:04:09.820
there's something to reach out to

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.097
and something to read about,

00:04:11.097 --> 00:04:13.048
at least the daily experience of it all.

00:04:13.048 --> 00:04:15.950
It's cool, it's cool
that it's actually within

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.783
a matter of months, it's helping people.

00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:20.826
Normally we're on the same
page about everything.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.359
And we're really good
at when the twins ask

00:04:22.359 --> 00:04:24.959
for something big that we
know they're gonna hold us to,

00:04:24.959 --> 00:04:27.861
we'll say, "Oh, I have to
talk to Charlotte first."

00:04:27.861 --> 00:04:30.439
Or she'll say, "Oh, I have
to talk to Isabel first."

00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:32.873
As long as we do that, we're fine.

00:04:32.873 --> 00:04:33.849
(laughs)

00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:35.311
- [Charlotte] I couldn't
imagine just not being

00:04:35.311 --> 00:04:37.076
part of this, to be honest.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.073
Me and Isabel definitely
had like our moments

00:04:39.073 --> 00:04:40.954
where we were like debating not living

00:04:40.954 --> 00:04:42.881
together in this situation.

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:44.625
The question was never,

00:04:44.625 --> 00:04:46.848
"Am I gonna leave the
raising the kids?" part,

00:04:46.848 --> 00:04:48.403
it's just, "How do we make it work?"

00:04:48.403 --> 00:04:49.820
where me and Isabel are in a situation

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.004
where we're getting along.

00:04:51.004 --> 00:04:52.954
- Charlotte and I have had our
ups and downs through this,

00:04:52.954 --> 00:04:54.510
but I don't know what I'd do without her.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.019
Like, we co-parent.

00:04:56.019 --> 00:04:57.528
I legally have guardianship,

00:04:57.528 --> 00:04:59.200
but it's a lot of work for one person.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.825
- I'm older by three minutes.

00:05:00.825 --> 00:05:01.777
He always says it's two,

00:05:01.777 --> 00:05:02.985
but I'm, it's three.

00:05:02.985 --> 00:05:03.937
- It's probably three.

00:05:03.937 --> 00:05:04.912
- It's three.

00:05:04.912 --> 00:05:06.282
- I think that at the beginning,

00:05:06.282 --> 00:05:08.302
it was really, you know,
learning how to make sure

00:05:08.302 --> 00:05:09.927
that all the bills were paid on time.

00:05:09.927 --> 00:05:12.040
And like, actually being head of household

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.175
rather than just a 23-year-old
girl with an apartment

00:05:15.175 --> 00:05:17.961
that I pay like rent,
electricity, and gas.

00:05:17.961 --> 00:05:20.538
You know, it's like now
there's budgeting for food,

00:05:20.538 --> 00:05:22.953
and budgeting for making sure

00:05:22.953 --> 00:05:24.532
that they have clothes on their backs,

00:05:24.532 --> 00:05:27.574
and random school projects that come up.

00:05:27.574 --> 00:05:31.126
Just making sure that all
of your ducks are in a row

00:05:31.126 --> 00:05:33.053
before you need them to be in a row,

00:05:33.053 --> 00:05:35.859
which is, it's daunting.

00:05:35.859 --> 00:05:38.483
- [Jasper] What about this one, Charlotte?

00:05:38.483 --> 00:05:39.899
- [Charlotte] That's
the one where Isabel's

00:05:39.899 --> 00:05:41.432
upset that I was being born.

00:05:41.432 --> 00:05:43.587
(all laugh)

00:05:43.587 --> 00:05:45.887
- [Isabel] I'm like, "Do
we have to keep her?"

00:05:47.037 --> 00:05:49.013
- My dad was the best dad.

00:05:49.013 --> 00:05:50.337
He didn't love anyone in the world

00:05:50.337 --> 00:05:51.753
more than he loved us.

00:05:51.753 --> 00:05:53.309
No matter where he was,
he was telling people

00:05:53.309 --> 00:05:54.725
about his kids and what they were up to,

00:05:54.725 --> 00:05:56.095
even when they didn't wanna listen.

00:05:56.095 --> 00:05:58.069
- At his funeral,
everyone's telling stories.

00:05:58.069 --> 00:05:59.833
And one person was like, "I
just remember this one time

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:01.505
"that we had a party bus,

00:06:01.505 --> 00:06:04.036
"and Harvey was like passing wine

00:06:04.036 --> 00:06:05.917
"out to the people on the street."

00:06:05.917 --> 00:06:07.844
He knew how to walk into
the room and own it,

00:06:07.844 --> 00:06:10.328
and how to talk to everybody,

00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:13.509
and how to make everyone
feel better about themselves.

00:06:13.509 --> 00:06:15.111
It was just, he was a cool dude.

00:06:15.111 --> 00:06:17.062
He was really fun, I miss him.

00:06:17.062 --> 00:06:19.453
- There's the thought
of what life should be

00:06:19.453 --> 00:06:22.425
versus what life is.

00:06:22.425 --> 00:06:24.794
But that's not a way to live a life.

00:06:24.794 --> 00:06:28.068
I just try to do as good
a job as he did for us

00:06:28.068 --> 00:06:31.777
with the twins, which is pretty high bar.

00:06:33.013 --> 00:06:34.639
- That was a cool video.

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:36.496
Colin's been working on
that for a long time.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:39.027
So next, I'm gonna go see
if Hillary wants to call

00:06:39.027 --> 00:06:43.131
her parents and ask them
another question about life.

00:06:45.064 --> 00:06:45.946
Hey guys.

00:06:45.946 --> 00:06:47.357
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:06:47.989 --> 00:06:50.979
(funky jazz music)

00:06:53.237 --> 00:06:55.344
- Calling Hillary's mom, you guys.

00:06:56.321 --> 00:06:58.639
- Very anti being in videos.

00:06:58.639 --> 00:06:59.591
- What up?

00:06:59.591 --> 00:07:00.613
- [Hillary] This is Henry.

00:07:00.613 --> 00:07:02.354
- [Henry] Hi, nice to meet you, Mrs. Rudy.

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:04.072
- Hi, Henry.

00:07:04.072 --> 00:07:05.489
- Do you want to switch the--

00:07:05.489 --> 00:07:07.973
we flip the phone so it's sideways.

00:07:07.973 --> 00:07:10.550
Yeah, perfect.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:15.101
So we're doing this
thing where we're having

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:17.609
people just call their
parents and ask them questions

00:07:17.609 --> 00:07:19.443
that they normally wouldn't ask.

00:07:19.443 --> 00:07:22.090
And Hillary has a question
which we picked out for her,

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:23.832
which she's gonna ask you.

00:07:23.832 --> 00:07:26.130
And then we'd just love
to hear your answer.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.500
- Okay.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.799
- Okay, how do you think you are different

00:07:29.799 --> 00:07:32.306
from me when you were my age?

00:07:32.306 --> 00:07:36.231
- Well, I was much more conservative.

00:07:36.231 --> 00:07:41.231
Much more concerned about
pleasing other people than myself,

00:07:41.385 --> 00:07:43.730
doing the right thing.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.163
And I was a lot straighter then.

00:07:47.163 --> 00:07:49.252
And, that's it.

00:07:49.252 --> 00:07:52.642
- Do you wish you had been
more like Hillary is now

00:07:52.642 --> 00:07:54.035
when you were her age?

00:07:54.035 --> 00:07:55.893
- I would love to be like Hillary.

00:07:55.893 --> 00:07:57.843
Every possible way.

00:07:57.843 --> 00:08:02.069
She's my idol, and I'm very,
very proud to be her mother.

00:08:02.069 --> 00:08:03.161
- Awwww.

00:08:03.161 --> 00:08:04.832
- Thanks, mom.

00:08:04.832 --> 00:08:06.411
- Cool, that's it, that's all we got.

00:08:06.411 --> 00:08:09.058
- I guess you've heard enough from me.

00:08:09.058 --> 00:08:10.196
- (both laugh) That was wonderful,

00:08:10.196 --> 00:08:11.496
thank you so much for doing this.

00:08:11.496 --> 00:08:13.191
- Good, well maybe you
won't call me for any more

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:15.211
of these videos in that case.

00:08:15.211 --> 00:08:16.604
(laughs)

00:08:16.604 --> 00:08:17.905
- Love you!

00:08:17.905 --> 00:08:19.182
- Ciao bella!

00:08:20.162 --> 00:08:23.311
- So, the next video is
a video that Jenny made

00:08:23.311 --> 00:08:25.934
about getting to know her family.

00:08:25.934 --> 00:08:27.606
Jenny, what was your video about?

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:30.114
- Well, I'm Cuban, my
whole family's Cuban.

00:08:30.114 --> 00:08:32.389
And my grandfather, along with my family,

00:08:32.389 --> 00:08:34.920
came to the states about 60 years ago,

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.262
and this is about finding
something that was once lost.

00:08:39.262 --> 00:08:41.236
(upbeat salsa music)

00:08:41.236 --> 00:08:42.629
- [Male Voice] Cuba, cuba.

00:08:42.629 --> 00:08:44.715
(laughter)

00:08:44.715 --> 00:08:46.480
- Ahhh.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.267
We have two ladies from Miami here

00:08:48.267 --> 00:08:50.450
to tell us a little bit about Cuban food.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.820
Dmitri and I--

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.399
- I'm just an idiot,
I don't know anything.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:54.908
- I'm an idiot, Dmitri's an idiot.

00:08:54.908 --> 00:08:56.928
We have never really
experienced Cuban food.

00:08:56.928 --> 00:08:58.461
We don't know what the
hell's going on here.

00:08:58.461 --> 00:09:00.365
I'm gonna eat off of all of
your plates, if that's alright.

00:09:00.365 --> 00:09:01.247
- Yeah, of course.

00:09:01.247 --> 00:09:02.315
- Allie, have you ever been to Cuba?

00:09:02.315 --> 00:09:03.313
- I have not.

00:09:03.313 --> 00:09:05.008
- And you have also not been to Cuba?

00:09:05.008 --> 00:09:07.237
- Some of my family
members are planning a trip

00:09:07.237 --> 00:09:09.327
in the not-too-distant future.

00:09:09.327 --> 00:09:11.092
So it's possible.

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:11.997
- Things are changing.

00:09:11.997 --> 00:09:14.342
- It's definitely something
I've wanted to do all my life.

00:09:14.342 --> 00:09:16.891
(upbeat salsa music)

00:09:20.403 --> 00:09:22.701
- So that sorta brings
us to why we're here.

00:09:22.701 --> 00:09:23.491
A couple of weeks ago,

00:09:23.491 --> 00:09:24.907
Jenny and I were on a shoot together

00:09:24.907 --> 00:09:27.275
for a video I was making
about meeting my neighbors.

00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:29.829
And, while we were stuck in
traffic and just chatting,

00:09:29.829 --> 00:09:32.058
Jenny mentioned to me that her grandfather

00:09:32.058 --> 00:09:33.335
used to be a painter,

00:09:33.335 --> 00:09:35.890
and that all of his paintings
were somewhere in Cuba,

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.422
and they had no idea where.

00:09:37.422 --> 00:09:40.232
- The local movie theaters
would hire him to draw like

00:09:40.232 --> 00:09:42.484
Clark Gable, and John Wayne,

00:09:42.484 --> 00:09:44.573
and all these famous American stars.

00:09:44.573 --> 00:09:46.524
They had to leave every single one

00:09:46.524 --> 00:09:49.124
with different neighbors
and family members

00:09:49.124 --> 00:09:50.518
scattered about Cuba.

00:09:50.518 --> 00:09:54.209
- And he's been gone since 1959, '58.

00:09:54.209 --> 00:09:56.090
- Yeah, since he took
that Peter Pan flight.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.599
- And now he's 93?

00:09:57.599 --> 00:09:59.782
- About to be 93 in August, yes.

00:09:59.782 --> 00:10:02.266
- So when he got to
America, what happened then?

00:10:02.266 --> 00:10:04.101
- He gave up painting.

00:10:04.101 --> 00:10:06.144
They weren't in a good position in Cuba,

00:10:06.144 --> 00:10:09.046
so it was a much worse situation in Miami.

00:10:09.046 --> 00:10:10.881
One of my cousins from Cuba,

00:10:10.881 --> 00:10:12.181
she got a Facebook account,

00:10:12.181 --> 00:10:13.481
and we just started talking.

00:10:13.481 --> 00:10:15.966
Found out that one of our neighbors kept

00:10:15.966 --> 00:10:20.470
probably the painting that meant
the most to my grandfather.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.815
(female voice speaking Spanish)

00:10:25.687 --> 00:10:27.725
(speaking Spanish)

00:11:06.735 --> 00:11:09.730
- [Jenny] Imagine, they
haven't talked to him in years.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.845
Like, the last time they saw him,

00:11:10.845 --> 00:11:13.167
he was like 26, like our age, you know.

00:11:13.167 --> 00:11:14.699
- Do you guys have any
questions at this point?

00:11:14.699 --> 00:11:15.953
- No, I mean, this is incredible.

00:11:15.953 --> 00:11:17.462
I'm just sorta like in awe right now.

00:11:17.462 --> 00:11:18.530
- Yeah, I'm riveted.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.759
- It turns out that he
drew this apparently

00:11:20.759 --> 00:11:22.199
when he was 17 years old.

00:11:22.199 --> 00:11:23.963
It was one of his first paintings.

00:11:23.963 --> 00:11:26.192
- He's 93 now, so that's like late '30s.

00:11:26.192 --> 00:11:29.861
- We have cousins that
moved to Miami from Cuba

00:11:29.861 --> 00:11:31.208
about five years ago,

00:11:31.208 --> 00:11:33.669
but they still travel frequently to Cuba.

00:11:33.669 --> 00:11:36.571
When we found out that the
painting was still in existence,

00:11:36.571 --> 00:11:38.104
we talked to him, and he's like,

00:11:38.104 --> 00:11:39.590
"Well, I'm going to a wedding."

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.378
He was very nervous about still trying

00:11:41.378 --> 00:11:43.467
to take that through the
airport with the frame.

00:11:43.467 --> 00:11:44.814
- 'Cause it's still like smuggling now.

00:11:44.814 --> 00:11:47.763
- When he rolled it up and
put it into a duffel bag,

00:11:47.763 --> 00:11:49.829
but then some funny things happened.

00:11:49.829 --> 00:11:51.339
- [Dmitri] There's more?

00:11:51.339 --> 00:11:53.057
- Yeah, this is when it gets weird.

00:11:53.057 --> 00:11:54.241
(Jenny laughs)

00:11:54.241 --> 00:11:57.747
- Just that short trip from Cuba to Miami,

00:11:57.747 --> 00:11:59.883
it broke into pieces.

00:11:59.883 --> 00:12:00.974
- Oh my god.

00:12:00.974 --> 00:12:02.251
- It was a jigsaw puzzle.

00:12:02.251 --> 00:12:04.504
My closest, closest, my bestest friend,

00:12:04.504 --> 00:12:06.501
was like, "Can you put this together?"

00:12:06.501 --> 00:12:08.288
Like, he did it in about three days,

00:12:08.288 --> 00:12:11.284
and there's that painting,
like on the table.

00:12:11.284 --> 00:12:12.746
And there was still pieces missing,

00:12:12.746 --> 00:12:13.884
like little scraps, we're like,

00:12:13.884 --> 00:12:16.717
"Oh, that's the end of the tail," or

00:12:16.717 --> 00:12:18.737
"That's the corner of this."

00:12:29.187 --> 00:12:31.407
(speaking Spanish)

00:12:43.858 --> 00:12:47.034
(upbeat salsa music)

00:12:49.195 --> 00:12:50.449
- [Jenny] My grandfather is a very,

00:12:50.449 --> 00:12:51.865
like he keeps his emotions to himself.

00:12:51.865 --> 00:12:53.182
And he was more quiet.

00:12:53.182 --> 00:12:55.225
But you could just read it off of him.

00:12:55.225 --> 00:12:57.292
- [Female Voice] Two, three, smile for me.

00:12:57.292 --> 00:12:58.499
(camera clicks) I love it.

00:12:58.499 --> 00:13:00.775
- [Jenny] He was just more
floored than anything.

00:13:02.035 --> 00:13:02.687
- My heart is pounding.

00:13:02.687 --> 00:13:03.477
Is it okay right now?

00:13:03.477 --> 00:13:04.522
Where is the painting right now?

00:13:04.522 --> 00:13:06.844
- It's hanging in my grandparent's house.

00:13:06.844 --> 00:13:08.028
- For your grandfather, this was something

00:13:08.028 --> 00:13:09.514
that his grandchild did.

00:13:09.514 --> 00:13:11.457
That now like another generation

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:12.943
is still connected to Cuba

00:13:12.943 --> 00:13:15.010
and is still connected to that root.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.262
I think that's really powerful.

00:13:17.262 --> 00:13:19.978
- Hey, and if anything changes
over the next couple years,

00:13:19.978 --> 00:13:21.766
Cuba might be a place you can go visit

00:13:21.766 --> 00:13:23.786
and see if you can find
some more of his paintings.

00:13:23.786 --> 00:13:24.878
You guys enjoy your food?

00:13:24.878 --> 00:13:26.039
- I'm not done yet.

00:13:26.039 --> 00:13:28.105
I was talking so much.
- You've been gabbing.

00:13:28.105 --> 00:13:29.614
You got all this food,

00:13:29.614 --> 00:13:31.727
we're in the clean plate club over here.

00:13:31.727 --> 00:13:34.142
- Come on, Jenny, eat up.

00:13:36.045 --> 00:13:37.061
- So now we're here with Curly.

00:13:37.061 --> 00:13:37.943
- Hey.

00:13:37.943 --> 00:13:41.194
- And Curly is going to call his mom.

00:13:41.194 --> 00:13:43.227
We just pulled him out of the kitchen.

00:13:43.227 --> 00:13:44.911
- Hi.
- [Curly] What's up?

00:13:45.481 --> 00:13:46.934
That's my little nephew.

00:13:46.934 --> 00:13:48.559
I have a question for you.

00:13:48.559 --> 00:13:50.161
- Hi, mom.

00:13:50.161 --> 00:13:51.462
- This is my co-worker.

00:13:51.462 --> 00:13:52.808
Alright, mom.

00:13:52.808 --> 00:13:53.784
What is something you would change

00:13:53.784 --> 00:13:55.618
about the way you raised me?

00:13:55.618 --> 00:13:56.756
- Uh, nothing.

00:13:56.756 --> 00:13:57.870
- Awwww.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.889
- Everything I did for you
is everything is excellent.

00:14:00.889 --> 00:14:02.467
- Awww, thanks mom.

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:03.489
Alright, one more question.

00:14:03.489 --> 00:14:06.090
How do you think love
changes over decades?

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.319
- Well, it changes, it changes a lot.

00:14:08.319 --> 00:14:11.012
You know, I mean, not being
married with my husband

00:14:11.012 --> 00:14:13.380
for 33 years now, you
know, you get married

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:17.583
for one day and two days, you divorce.

00:14:17.583 --> 00:14:20.021
- My mom's a big fan of Kim Kardashian.

00:14:20.021 --> 00:14:21.971
- What's the secret, what did you guys do?

00:14:21.971 --> 00:14:23.132
- What's the secret?

00:14:23.132 --> 00:14:26.197
Well, you know, I love him since,

00:14:26.197 --> 00:14:28.821
I love him now like I met him yesterday.

00:14:28.821 --> 00:14:30.470
- That's sweet, mom.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:32.893
Alrighty, mom.

00:14:32.893 --> 00:14:34.472
- [Henry] That was
great, thank you so much.

00:14:34.472 --> 00:14:35.981
- Thanks mom, bye Noah.

00:14:35.981 --> 00:14:36.981
I love you, bye mom.

00:14:36.981 --> 00:14:38.467
- I love you too, bye-bye!

00:14:38.467 --> 00:14:39.764
- Cool, that was wondeful.

00:14:39.764 --> 00:14:40.530
- Thanks.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:41.436
- I mean, do you feel like,

00:14:41.436 --> 00:14:42.806
do you wish you talk to your mom,

00:14:42.806 --> 00:14:45.283
you like ask questions
like that more often?

00:14:45.283 --> 00:14:46.584
- Oh yeah, my mom yeah,

00:14:46.584 --> 00:14:47.489
my mom might have--

00:14:47.489 --> 00:14:48.511
I'm super tight with my dad,

00:14:48.511 --> 00:14:51.018
but me and my mom are
like a little different.

00:14:51.018 --> 00:14:51.947
- [Henry] Think about that.

00:14:51.947 --> 00:14:53.572
Think about the questions you wish

00:14:53.572 --> 00:14:54.916
you could ask your parents,

00:14:54.916 --> 00:14:56.866
and then maybe just ask them.

00:14:56.866 --> 00:14:57.946
- Yeah, I agree with that.

00:14:57.946 --> 00:14:59.107
- Call 'em and ask.

00:14:59.107 --> 00:15:00.556
- It's good for your grandparents too.

00:15:00.556 --> 00:15:01.972
I do that with my grandma actually.

00:15:01.972 --> 00:15:03.807
- Yeah, if your grandparents
are still with you,

00:15:03.807 --> 00:15:05.316
don't take that for granted.

00:15:05.316 --> 00:15:08.729
And with that, we'll end
this episode of Real Mature.

00:15:08.729 --> 00:15:10.262
What a do.

00:15:10.262 --> 00:15:11.167
- Yay!

00:15:11.167 --> 00:15:12.003
- Say "What a do."

00:15:12.003 --> 00:15:12.885
- What a do!

00:15:12.885 --> 00:15:14.720
- What a do!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.904
You guys say "What a do" too.

00:15:15.904 --> 00:15:17.343
- What a do.
- What a do.

